 Mastering Jenkins Pipelines – Declarative vs Scripted 🚀

In Jenkins, Pipelines are the heart of CI/CD automation. But did you know there are two main types?

Let’s break it down 👇

💡 Declarative Pipeline
✅ More structured & user-friendly
✅ Ideal for teams & large projects
✅ Easier syntax, great for beginners

pipeline {
 agent any
 stages {
 stage('Build') {
 steps {
 echo 'Building...'
 }
 }
 }
}

💻 Scripted Pipeline
✅ More powerful & flexible
✅ Closer to traditional programming
✅ Perfect for advanced users

node {
 stage('Build') {
 echo 'Building...'
 }
}

🎯 When to Use What?
 • If you’re new to Jenkins or need a clean structure: Declarative
 • If you need full control or complex logic: Scripted

⚙️ Pro Tip: I often combine both styles strategically in my real-world Jenkins implementations!
